            <ArticleTitle>The significance of the axial foot projection in the diagnosis of metatarsal pathology.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>139-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Metatarsalgia is a symptom and not a disease. Three cases, as examples, are presented to highlight the need for axial roentgenograms of the forefoot in order to elicit the pathology missed by regular posterior-anterior and lateral roentgenograms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
